<p>
	Every setting can be overridden for a project and its subprojects with a
	<%= link_to "project custom field", new_custom_field_path(:type => "ProjectCustomField") %>
	named "Google Chat" and the setting name without "?", e.g. "Google Chat Post Issue Updates":
	a boolean field for the yes/no settings, a long text field for "Ignored Fields" and a text field for the others.
	Empty values use the setting of the parent project or of the plugin.
</p>

<p>
	<label for="settings_hangouts_chat_url">Google Chat URL</label>
	<input type="text" id="settings_hangouts_chat_url" size="80" value="<%= settings['hangouts_chat_url'] %>" name="settings[hangouts_chat_url]" />
	<em class="info">Webhook URL of the Google Chat space.</em>
</p>

<p>
	<label for="settings_thread">Google Chat Thread</label>
	<input type="text" id="settings_thread" value="<%= settings['thread'] %>" name="settings[thread]" />
	<em class="info">
		Without a thread, every message is posted on its own.
		The thread "-" disables the messages; in a project, not those of its subprojects.
	</em>
</p>

<p>
	<label for="settings_thread_per_issue">One Thread per Issue?</label>
	<input type="checkbox" id="settings_thread_per_issue" value="1" name="settings[thread_per_issue]" <%= settings['thread_per_issue'] == '1' ? 'checked="checked"' : '' %> />
	<em class="info">
		Posts all messages about an issue to the thread "&lt;thread&gt;-issue-&lt;id&gt;", or "redmine-issue-&lt;id&gt;" without a thread.
		Wiki updates stay in the thread.
	</em>
</p>

<p>
	<label for="settings_display_watchers">Display Watchers?</label>
	<select id="settings_display_watchers" name="settings[display_watchers]">
		<option value="yes" <%= settings['display_watchers'] == 'yes' ? 'selected="selected"' : '' %>>Yes</option>
		<option value="no" <%= settings['display_watchers'] != 'yes' ? 'selected="selected"' : '' %>>No</option>
	</select>
	<em class="info">Lists the watchers in messages about new issues.</em>
</p>

<p>
	<label for="settings_post_updates">Post Issue Updates?</label>
	<input type="checkbox" id="settings_post_updates" value="1" name="settings[post_updates]" <%= settings['post_updates'] == '1' ? 'checked="checked"' : '' %> />
	<em class="info">New issues are always posted.</em>
</p>

<p>
	<label for="settings_post_wiki_updates">Post Wiki Updates?</label>
	<input type="checkbox" id="settings_post_wiki_updates" value="1" name="settings[post_wiki_updates]" <%= settings['post_wiki_updates'] == '1' ? 'checked="checked"' : '' %> />
</p>

<p>
	<label for="settings_ignored_fields">Ignored Fields</label>
	<textarea id="settings_ignored_fields" rows="4" cols="40" name="settings[ignored_fields]"><%= settings['ignored_fields'] %></textarea>
	<em class="info">
		Changes to these fields are not posted, one field per line. Use the name of a custom field or of an issue attribute.
		Updates which only change ignored fields and have no notes are not sent at all.
	</em>
</p>

<p>
	<label for="settings_order_approval">Order Approval?</label>
	<input type="checkbox" id="settings_order_approval" value="1" name="settings[order_approval]" <%= settings['order_approval'] == '1' ? 'checked="checked"' : '' %> />
	<em class="info">Issues whose subject contains "Bestellung" get a button to approve them, and chat messages about them a "Freigeben" button.</em>
</p>
